<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<System>
  <P Name="Location">[1681, 561, 2815, 1548]</P>
  <P Name="PaperType">usletter</P>
  <Block BlockType="M-S-Function" Name="Application CPU load" SID="4353">
    <PortCounts out="1"/>
    <P Name="Position">[715, 373, 865, 417]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">719</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_gocontroll_cpu_load</P>
    <P Name="Parameters">tsamp</P>
    <Mask SelfModifiable="on">
      <Type>Application CPU load</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;Application CPU load&apos;);
text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Application CPU Load&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
This block provides the current CPU load of the Moduline S1 application.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
The reported value represents the processor usage of the running
application and can be used to monitor system performance.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
It is intended for diagnostic and performance analysis purposes during
development and runtime monitoring.
&lt;/p&gt;</Description>
      <Initialization>mdl = bdroot;
cs  = getActiveConfigSet(mdl);
try
t = go_target_name(get_param(cs,&apos;tlcGOcontrollTarget&apos;));
catch
t = &quot;Unknown controller&quot;;
end
msk = Simulink.Mask.get(gcb);
c = msk.getParameter(&apos;ContrType&apos;);
c.Value = t;</Initialization>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Application CPU load&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Outputs how much of the processor time the application uses, in percent.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use it during development to check that the application has room to spare.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;On a Linux controller the output is 0.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Moduline S1. On the Linux controllers the output is 0. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/external-monitoring/&quot;&gt;Monitoring a signal with HANtune over XCP&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/external-monitoring/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="ContrType" Type="edit" Evaluate="off" Enabled="off">
        <Prompt>Controller type</Prompt>
        <Value>Unknown controller</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="tsamp" Type="edit" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
        <Value>1</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Parameters</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="ContrType">
          <Prompt>Controller type</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="tsamp">
          <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
  </Block>
  <Block BlockType="M-S-Function" Name="Application available stack" SID="4351">
    <PortCounts out="1"/>
    <P Name="Position">[515, 373, 665, 417]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">717</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_gocontroll_model_stack</P>
    <P Name="Parameters">tsamp</P>
    <Mask SelfModifiable="on">
      <Type>Application available stack</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;Available stack monitor&apos;);
text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Available Stack Monitor&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
This block provides the remaining available stack memory of the running application.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
It can be used to monitor stack usage during development and to detect potential
stack overflow conditions.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
This functionality is only available on Moduline S1 controllers.
&lt;/p&gt;</Description>
      <Initialization>mdl = bdroot;
cs  = getActiveConfigSet(mdl);
try
t = go_target_name(get_param(cs,&apos;tlcGOcontrollTarget&apos;));
catch
t = &quot;Unknown controller&quot;;
end
msk = Simulink.Mask.get(gcb);
c = msk.getParameter(&apos;ContrType&apos;);
c.Value = t;</Initialization>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Application available stack&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Outputs how much stack memory of the application is still unused.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use it during development. When it comes close to 0, enlarge the stack with the &lt;i&gt;RAM configuration&lt;/i&gt; block.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;On a Linux controller the output is 0.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Moduline S1. On the Linux controllers the output is 0. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/external-monitoring/&quot;&gt;Monitoring a signal with HANtune over XCP&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/external-monitoring/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="ContrType" Type="edit" Evaluate="off" Enabled="off">
        <Prompt>Controller type</Prompt>
        <Value>Unknown controller</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="tsamp" Type="edit" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
        <Value>1</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Parameters</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="ContrType">
          <Prompt>Controller type</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="tsamp">
          <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
  </Block>
  <Block BlockType="M-S-Function" Name="Application free heap" SID="4352">
    <PortCounts out="1"/>
    <P Name="Position">[715, 288, 865, 332]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">718</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_gocontroll_free_heap</P>
    <P Name="Parameters">tsamp</P>
    <Mask SelfModifiable="on">
      <Type>Application free heap</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;Application free heap&apos;);
text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Application Heap&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
This block provides information about the available heap memory of the
Moduline S1 application.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
The reported value reflects the remaining dynamic memory that can be
allocated during runtime.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
It can be used to monitor memory usage and to detect potential memory
exhaustion during development and operation.
&lt;/p&gt;</Description>
      <Initialization>mdl = bdroot;
cs  = getActiveConfigSet(mdl);
try
t = go_target_name(get_param(cs,&apos;tlcGOcontrollTarget&apos;));
catch
t = &quot;Unknown controller&quot;;
end
msk = Simulink.Mask.get(gcb);
c = msk.getParameter(&apos;ContrType&apos;);
c.Value = t;</Initialization>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Application free heap&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Outputs how much heap memory is free.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use it during development: a value that keeps falling means the application runs out of memory.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;On a Linux controller the output is 0.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Moduline S1. On the Linux controllers the output is 0. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/external-monitoring/&quot;&gt;Monitoring a signal with HANtune over XCP&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/external-monitoring/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="ContrType" Type="edit" Evaluate="off" Enabled="off">
        <Prompt>Controller type</Prompt>
        <Value>Unknown controller</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="tsamp" Type="edit" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
        <Value>1</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Parameters</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="ContrType">
          <Prompt>Controller type</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="tsamp">
          <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
  </Block>
  <Block BlockType="M-S-Function" Name="Controller temperature" SID="4099">
    <PortCounts out="1"/>
    <P Name="Position">[515, 288, 665, 332]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">528</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_gocontroll_controller_temperature</P>
    <P Name="Parameters">tsamp</P>
    <Mask SelfModifiable="on">
      <Type>Controller temperature</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;Contoller temperature&apos;);
text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Controller Temperature&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
This block provides the internal controller temperature measured by the
integrated temperature sensor.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
The sensor is embedded inside the controller and reflects the internal
operating temperature of the device.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
The reported temperature does not represent ambient temperature, as it is
influenced by internal heat dissipation and system load.
&lt;/p&gt;</Description>
      <Initialization>% Get model context and target (t)
mdl = bdroot;
cs  = getActiveConfigSet(mdl);
try
t = go_target_name(get_param(cs,&apos;tlcGOcontrollTarget&apos;));
catch
t = &quot;Unknown controller&quot;;
end
msk = Simulink.Mask.get(gcb);
c = msk.getParameter(&apos;ContrType&apos;);
c.Value = t;</Initialization>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Controller temperature&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Measures the temperature inside the controller.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;This is the temperature of the electronics, not of the surroundings: it is higher than the ambient temperature.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use it to guard the controller, for example to reduce the load when it gets hot.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;All controllers: Moduline S1, M1, L4 and HMI1. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/s1/&quot;&gt;Moduline S1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/s1/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/m1/&quot;&gt;Moduline M1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/m1/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/l4/&quot;&gt;Moduline L4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/l4/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/hmi1/&quot;&gt;Moduline HMI1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/hmi1/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="ContrType" Type="edit" Enabled="off">
        <Prompt>Controller type</Prompt>
        <Value>Unknown controller</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="tsamp" Type="edit" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
        <Value>1</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Parameters</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="ContrType">
          <Prompt>Controller type</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="tsamp">
          <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
  </Block>
  <Block BlockType="M-S-Function" Name="Execute shell command" SID="4100">
    <PortCounts in="1"/>
    <P Name="Position">[515, 85, 665, 135]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">529</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <List ListType="RTWdata">
      <P Name="command">command</P>
    </List>
    <P Name="CopyFcn">go_block_platform_check(gcb, &apos;Linux&apos;, &apos;notify&apos;);</P>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_exec_shell</P>
    <Mask>
      <Type>Execute shell command</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&quot;Execute command:\n%s&quot;,command);
text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>Execute a Linux Shell command when the input is true.

Accepts a Boolean input, use a triggered subsystem to call the function only once on a state change instead of every sample.&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;For the Linux controllers (Moduline M1, L4, HMI1) only.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</Description>
      <Initialization>go_block_platform_check(gcb, &apos;Linux&apos;);
    if ~ischar(command)
        error(&apos;Given command is not a string&apos;);
    end

    %update RTWdata so WriteRTW gets called again
    modelRTWFields = struct(&apos;command&apos;, command);

    % Insert modelRTWFields in the I/O block S-Function containing the Tag starting with &apos;HANcoder_TARGET_&apos;
    HANcoder_TARGET_DataBlock = find_system(gcb, &apos;RegExp&apos;, &apos;on&apos;, &apos;FollowLinks&apos;, &apos;on&apos;, &apos;LookUnderMasks&apos;, &apos;all&apos;, &apos;BlockType&apos;, &apos;M-S-Function&apos;);
    set_param(HANcoder_TARGET_DataBlock{1}, &apos;RTWdata&apos;, modelRTWFields);</Initialization>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Execute shell command&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Runs a Linux command on the controller while its input is true.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Command&lt;/b&gt;: the command line, as you would type it in a terminal on the controller.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;While the input is true the command is started again every sample. Put the block in a triggered subsystem to run it once.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The command is started in the background: the application does not wait for it and does not get its result.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Linux controllers only: Moduline M1, L4 and HMI1. In a model for the Moduline S1 the block gives an error. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="command" Type="edit" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Command:</Prompt>
        <Value>&apos;command&apos;</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Parameters</Prompt>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="command">
        <Prompt>Command:</Prompt>
        <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
  </Block>
  <Block BlockType="M-S-Function" Name="RAM configuration" SID="4345">
    <PortCounts out="2"/>
    <P Name="Position">[510, 1056, 665, 1129]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">716</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <List ListType="RTWdata">
      <P Name="mainStack">2048</P>
    </List>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_ram</P>
    <Mask>
      <Type>RAM configuration</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;Stack config&apos;);

port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 1, &apos;Free main stack&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 2, &apos;Free heap&apos;);

text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>Set the Stack size for the main thread and read available memory in the stack and heap.</Description>
      <Initialization>if (mainStack &lt; 2048)
    error(&apos;The main stack should be at least 2kB&apos;);
end

modelRTWFields = struct(&apos;mainStack&apos;,int2str(mainStack));

set_param(gcb, &apos;RTWdata&apos;, modelRTWFields);</Initialization>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;RAM configuration&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sets the stack size of the application on the Moduline S1 and outputs the free stack and free heap.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Main stack size (bytes)&lt;/b&gt;: default 2048. Enlarge it when the free stack output comes close to 0, for example in a large model.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;On a Linux controller the block does nothing.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Moduline S1. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/s1/&quot;&gt;Moduline S1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/s1/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="mainStack" Type="edit">
        <Prompt>Main stack size (bytes)</Prompt>
        <Value>2048</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Parameters</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="mainStack">
          <Prompt>Main stack size (bytes)</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
  </Block>
  <Block BlockType="M-S-Function" Name="Read GPS" SID="4344">
    <PortCounts out="11"/>
    <P Name="Position">[510, 791, 665, 999]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">715</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_gps</P>
    <Mask>
      <Type>Read gps</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;Read GPS&apos;);

port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 1, &apos;longitude&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 2, &apos;latitude&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 3, &apos;altitude&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 4, &apos;velocity&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 5, &apos;year&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 6, &apos;month&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 7, &apos;day&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 8, &apos;hour&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 9, &apos;minute&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 10, &apos;second&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 11, &apos;valid&apos;);

text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>Reads several data points from an installed 4G/GPS module.

latitude/longitude in degrees
altitude in meters
velocity in meters per second

Southern hemisphere is negative latitude
Western hemisphere is negative longitude

The date/time is in UTC

All outputs are 0 untill a connection to a gps satelite is made.
When it fails to read a valid value from the gps module it also outputs all 0.</Description>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Read gps&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reads the position and time from the GPS receiver of the controller.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Outputs: longitude and latitude in degrees (west and south are negative), altitude (m), velocity (m/s), date and time (UTC), and &lt;b&gt;valid&lt;/b&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;All outputs are 0 until the receiver has a fix. Use the output &lt;b&gt;valid&lt;/b&gt; before you use the position.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The controller needs the GPS option and an antenna with a view of the sky. Only one block per model.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;All controllers: Moduline S1, M1, L4 and HMI1. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/s1/&quot;&gt;Moduline S1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/s1/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/m1/&quot;&gt;Moduline M1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/m1/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/l4/&quot;&gt;Moduline L4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/l4/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/hmi1/&quot;&gt;Moduline HMI1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/hmi1/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
  </Block>
  <Block BlockType="M-S-Function" Name="Read RTC" SID="4401">
    <PortCounts out="6"/>
    <P Name="Position">[750, 793, 905, 1002]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">720</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_gocontroll_rtc</P>
    <P Name="Parameters">tsamp</P>
    <Mask SelfModifiable="on">
      <Type>Read gps</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;Read RTC&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 1, &apos;year&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 2, &apos;month&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 3, &apos;day&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 4, &apos;hour&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 5, &apos;minute&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 6, &apos;second&apos;);

text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>Reads several data points from an installed 4G/GPS module.

latitude/longitude in degrees
altitude in meters
velocity in meters per second

Southern hemisphere is negative latitude
Western hemisphere is negative longitude

The date/time is in UTC

All outputs are 0 untill a connection to a gps satelite is made.
When it fails to read a valid value from the gps module it also outputs all 0.</Description>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Read gps&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reads the date and time of the real-time clock of the controller.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Outputs: year, month, day, hour, minute and second.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Only one block per model.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;All controllers: Moduline S1, M1, L4 and HMI1. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="tsamp" Type="edit">
        <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
        <Value>1</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="Container2">
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="tsamp">
          <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
  </Block>
  <Block BlockType="M-S-Function" Name="Read accelerometer" SID="4299">
    <PortCounts out="6"/>
    <P Name="Position">[505, 641, 670, 759]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">714</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <List ListType="RTWdata">
      <P Name="sampling_frequency">1</P>
      <P Name="scale">0</P>
    </List>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_read_accel</P>
    <P Name="Parameters">tsamp</P>
    <Mask SelfModifiable="on">
      <Type>Read accelerometer</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;Read accelerometer\nChip sampling frequency: %s Hz&apos;, get_param(gcb,&apos;sampling_frequency&apos;));

port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 1, &apos;Acc X&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 2, &apos;Acc Y&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 3, &apos;Acc Z&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 4, &apos;Gyro X&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 5, &apos;Gyro Y&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 6, &apos;Gyro Z&apos;);

text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>This block reads out the accelerometer embedded into several Moduline controllers

Moduline M1 3 axis acceleration measurement
Moduline S1 3 axis acceleration measurement with 3 axis gyroscopes

It outputs the acceleration in all 3 spatial dimensons in m/s^2.

Positive X axis is acceleration towards the connectors in the length of the controller
Positive Y axis is acceleration towards the empty side of the controller, so opposite of the two m12 connectors
Positive Z axis is acceleration straight up if the controller was lying on its back so towards the indicator leds</Description>
      <Initialization>
    % Get model context and target (t)
    mdl = bdroot;
    cs  = getActiveConfigSet(mdl);
    try
    t = go_target_name(get_param(cs,&apos;tlcGOcontrollTarget&apos;));
    catch
    t = &quot;Unknown controller&quot;;
    end
    % Get mask context
    msk = Simulink.Mask.get(gcb);
    a = msk.getParameter(&apos;accel_description&apos;);

 
    if contains(t,&apos;Moduline S1&apos;)
        %a.Value  = &apos;Moduline_Mini_I_Accelerometer_3D_Axis.svg&apos;;
    else
        %a.TypeOptions = &apos;Moduline_Mini_I_Accelerometer_3D_Axis.svg&apos;;
    end

modelRTWFields = struct(&apos;sampling_frequency&apos;,int2str(sampling_frequency-1), &apos;scale&apos;, int2str(scale-1));

set_param(gcb, &apos;RTWdata&apos;, modelRTWFields);
</Initialization>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Read accelerometer&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reads the motion sensor of the controller: acceleration in X, Y and Z (m/s2) and, on the Moduline S1, rotation in X, Y and Z.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Chip sampling frequency&lt;/b&gt;: 1 to 200 Hz. &lt;b&gt;Sensitivity&lt;/b&gt;: 2G, 4G, 8G or 16G; a lower range gives a finer resolution.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Positive X points to the connectors, positive Z to the indicator LEDs.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The Moduline M1 gives acceleration only. Only one block per model.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Moduline S1 (acceleration and rotation) and Moduline M1 (acceleration). The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/s1/&quot;&gt;Moduline S1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/s1/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/m1/&quot;&gt;Moduline M1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/m1/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="tsamp" Type="edit" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
        <Value>0.1</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="sampling_frequency" Type="popup" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Chip sampling frequency in Hz</Prompt>
        <Value>12</Value>
        <TypeOptions>
          <Option>1</Option>
          <Option>12</Option>
          <Option>25</Option>
          <Option>50</Option>
          <Option>100</Option>
          <Option>200</Option>
        </TypeOptions>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="scale" Type="popup" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Sensitivity</Prompt>
        <Value>-2G/2G</Value>
        <TypeOptions>
          <Option>-2G/2G</Option>
          <Option>-4G/4G</Option>
          <Option>-8G/8G</Option>
          <Option>-16G/16G</Option>
        </TypeOptions>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Image" Name="accel_description">
        <FilePath>Moduline_Mini_I_Accelerometer_3D_Axis.svg</FilePath>
        <ControlOptions HorizontalStretch="off"/>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Parameters</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="tsamp">
          <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Popup" Name="sampling_frequency">
          <Prompt>Chip sampling frequency in Hz</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Popup" Name="scale">
          <Prompt>Sensitivity</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
    <PortProperties>
      <Port Type="out" Index="1">
        <P Name="Name">accel_x</P>
      </Port>
      <Port Type="out" Index="2">
        <P Name="Name">accel_y</P>
      </Port>
      <Port Type="out" Index="3">
        <P Name="Name">accel_z</P>
      </Port>
    </PortProperties>
  </Block>
  <Block BlockType="M-S-Function" Name="Software version" SID="4277">
    <PortCounts out="3"/>
    <P Name="Position">[505, 560, 675, 610]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">700</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <List ListType="RTWdata">
      <P Name="major">0</P>
      <P Name="minor">0</P>
      <P Name="patch">1</P>
    </List>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_software_version</P>
    <P Name="Parameters">major, minor, patch</P>
    <Mask SelfModifiable="on">
      <Type>Software version</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;Model V%s.%s.%s&apos;, int2str(major), int2str(minor), int2str(patch));
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 1, &apos;Major&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 2, &apos;Minor&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 3, &apos;Patch&apos;);
text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Software version&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
This block defines the software version of the model.
The version follows semantic versioning (&lt;b&gt;Major.Minor.Patch&lt;/b&gt;).
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
The three version numbers are available as output signals for use in the model,
for example via HANtune measurements or CAN messages.
They are also stored in the controller info for later retrieval.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Outputs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Major&lt;/b&gt; &amp;mdash; Incremented on breaking changes or major new functionality.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Minor&lt;/b&gt; &amp;mdash; Incremented on new features, backwards compatible.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;b&gt;Patch&lt;/b&gt; &amp;mdash; Incremented on bug fixes, backwards compatible.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
Only one Software version block should be present in the model.&lt;br/&gt;
Each version field must be an integer in the range 0&amp;ndash;255.
&lt;/p&gt;</Description>
      <Initialization>
mdl = bdroot;
cs  = getActiveConfigSet(mdl);
try
    t = go_target_name(get_param(cs, &apos;tlcGOcontrollTarget&apos;));
catch
    t = &quot;Unknown controller&quot;;
end
msk = Simulink.Mask.get(gcb);
c = msk.getParameter(&apos;ContrType&apos;);
c.Value = t;

if mod(major, 1) &gt; 0
    error(&quot;Major must be an integer value&quot;);
end
if mod(minor, 1) &gt; 0
    error(&quot;Minor must be an integer value&quot;);
end
if mod(patch, 1) &gt; 0
    error(&quot;Patch must be an integer value&quot;);
end

modelRTWFields = struct(&apos;major&apos;, int2str(major), ...
    &apos;minor&apos;, int2str(minor), ...
    &apos;patch&apos;, int2str(patch));
set_param(gcb, &apos;RTWdata&apos;, modelRTWFields);
</Initialization>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Software version&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Gives the application a version number.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Major&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;b&gt;Minor&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;b&gt;Patch&lt;/b&gt;: numbers from 0 to 255. They are also the three outputs of the block.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The version is stored with the application on the controller, so you can read which application runs, and it is part of the name of the build result.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Raise the version with every release. Only one block per model.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;All controllers: Moduline S1, M1, L4 and HMI1. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/upload/&quot;&gt;Upload the application&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/upload/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="ContrType" Type="edit" Evaluate="off" Enabled="off">
        <Prompt>Controller type</Prompt>
        <Value>Unknown controller</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="major" Type="edit">
        <Prompt>Major:</Prompt>
        <Value>0</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="minor" Type="edit">
        <Prompt>Minor:</Prompt>
        <Value>0</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="patch" Type="edit">
        <Prompt>Patch:</Prompt>
        <Value>1</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Parameters</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="ContrType">
          <Prompt>Controller type</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="major">
          <Prompt>Major:</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="minor">
          <Prompt>Minor:</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions Row="current" PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="patch">
          <Prompt>Patch:</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions Row="current" PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
    <PortProperties>
      <Port Type="out" Index="1">
        <P Name="Name">Major</P>
      </Port>
      <Port Type="out" Index="2">
        <P Name="Name">Minor</P>
      </Port>
      <Port Type="out" Index="3">
        <P Name="Name">Patch</P>
      </Port>
    </PortProperties>
  </Block>
  <Block BlockType="M-S-Function" Name="XCP Server" SID="4228">
    <PortCounts/>
    <P Name="Position">[515, 459, 665, 511]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">531</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <P Name="Priority">999999</P>
    <List ListType="RTWdata">
      <P Name="server_type">1</P>
      <P Name="receive_id">1637</P>
      <P Name="receive_id_ext">0</P>
      <P Name="send_id">1638</P>
      <P Name="send_id_ext">0</P>
      <P Name="can_if">0</P>
    </List>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_xcp_server</P>
    <Mask SelfModifiable="on">
      <Type>XCP Server</Type>
      <Display IconUnits="pixels">if ContrType == &quot;Unknown controller&quot;
fprintf(&apos;XCP Server&apos;);
else

type = get_param(gcb,&apos;server_type&apos;);
if (strcmp(type, &apos;CAN&apos;))
    fprintf(&apos;XCP Server\n%s&apos;, get_param(gcb,&apos;can_if&apos;));
else
    fprintf(&apos;XCP Server\n%s&apos;, type);
end
end
text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;XCP Server&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
Adding one block of this type to the model enables the integrated XCP server,
allowing calibration and measurement via HANtune.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
Only one XCP Server block should be present in the model.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
Moduline S1 supports XCP over CAN or over Bluetooth. Over Bluetooth the XCP
packets travel through the ESP32 to a host such as the GOcontroll Monitor;
the A2L file is the same.
&lt;/p&gt;</Description>
      <Initialization>
mdl = bdroot;
cs  = getActiveConfigSet(mdl);
try
t = go_target_name(get_param(cs,&apos;tlcGOcontrollTarget&apos;));
catch
t = &quot;Unknown controller&quot;;
end
msk = Simulink.Mask.get(gcb);
c = msk.getParameter(&apos;ContrType&apos;);
s = msk.getParameter(&apos;server_type&apos;);
ca = msk.getParameter(&apos;can_if&apos;);
c.Value = t;

if contains(t,&apos;Unknown controller&apos;)
 s.Visible = &apos;off&apos;;  
else
 s.Visible = &apos;on&apos;;  
end

% Moduline S1: CAN or Bluetooth. The other controllers: TCP, UDP or CAN.
s.Enabled = &apos;on&apos;;
if contains(t,&apos;Moduline S1&apos;)
    if ~any(strcmp(s.Value, {&apos;CAN&apos;,&apos;Bluetooth&apos;}))
        s.Value = &apos;CAN&apos;;
    end
elseif ~contains(t,&apos;Unknown controller&apos;) &amp;&amp; strcmp(s.Value, &apos;Bluetooth&apos;)
    s.Value = &apos;TCP&apos;;
end
server_type = find(strcmp(s.TypeOptions, s.Value));

if contains(t,&apos;Moduline S1&apos;)||contains(t,&apos;Moduline HMI1&apos;)
    ca.TypeOptions = {&apos;CAN1 - Connector pin 16 (L) and pin 17 (H)&apos;,&apos;CAN2 - Connector pin 24 (L) and pin 25 (H)&apos;};
elseif contains(t,&apos;Moduline M1&apos;)
    ca.TypeOptions = {&apos;CAN1 - Connector B pin 24 (L) and pin 25 (H)&apos;,&apos;CAN2 - Connector A pin 24 (L) and pin 25 (H)&apos;};
elseif contains(t,&apos;Moduline L4&apos;)
    ca.TypeOptions = {&apos;CAN1 - Connector C pin 14 (L) and pin 15 (H)&apos;,&apos;CAN2 - Connector C pin 20 (L) and pin 21 (H)&apos;,&apos;CAN3 - Connector C pin 19 (L) and pin 18 (H)&apos;,&apos;CAN4 - Connector C pin 13 (L) and pin 12 (H)&apos;};
end

    if ~receive_id_ext &amp;&amp; receive_id &gt; hex2dec(&apos;7ff&apos;)
        error(&quot;The given receive ID is too large for a standard ID, select the extended ID option for extended IDs&quot;);
    end

    if ~send_id_ext &amp;&amp; send_id &gt; hex2dec(&apos;7ff&apos;)
        error(&quot;The given send ID is too large for a standard ID, select the extended ID option for extended IDs&quot;);
    end

    % The number of the bus comes from its name (CAN1, CAN2, ...): the variable can_if was
    % worked out before the list above was set, so it can still count in the list of the library.
    can_if = sscanf(get_param(gcb, &apos;can_if&apos;), &apos;CAN%d&apos;, 1);
    if isempty(can_if), can_if = 1; end
    %update RTWdata here so the WriteRTW callback gets run again
    modelRTWFields = struct(&apos;server_type&apos;, int2str(server_type), ...
        &apos;receive_id&apos;, int2str(receive_id), ...
        &apos;receive_id_ext&apos;, int2str(receive_id_ext), ...
        &apos;send_id&apos;, int2str(send_id), ...
        &apos;send_id_ext&apos;, int2str(send_id_ext),...
        &apos;can_if&apos;, int2str(can_if-1));

    set_param(gcb, &apos;RTWdata&apos;, modelRTWFields);</Initialization>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;XCP Server&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Switches on the XCP server of the application, so a tool such as HANtune can measure signals and change parameters while the application runs. Each build makes an A2L file that describes them.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Server type&lt;/b&gt;: how the tool connects. Moduline S1: CAN or Bluetooth. Linux controllers: TCP, UDP or CAN.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;For CAN: the &lt;b&gt;CAN bus&lt;/b&gt;, the &lt;b&gt;Receive ID&lt;/b&gt; (default 0x665) and the &lt;b&gt;Send ID&lt;/b&gt; (default 0x666); tick &lt;b&gt;Extended ID&lt;/b&gt; for an identifier above 0x7FF.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;For TCP and UDP the address and port are set under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options&lt;/i&gt;. Fill in the IP address of the controller.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A &lt;b&gt;signal&lt;/b&gt; appears in the A2L file when its line has a name and the storage class ExportedGlobal. A &lt;b&gt;parameter&lt;/b&gt; appears when it is a Simulink.Parameter with storage class ExportedGlobal.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The model needs at least one such signal, otherwise the connection with HANtune times out.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Only one XCP Server block per model.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;All controllers: Moduline S1, M1, L4 and HMI1. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/external-monitoring/&quot;&gt;Monitoring a signal with HANtune over XCP&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/external-monitoring/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/external-control/&quot;&gt;Controlling a model with HANtune over XCP&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/external-control/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/exchange-with-node-red/&quot;&gt;Exchange data with Node-RED&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/exchange-with-node-red/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="ContrType" Type="edit" Evaluate="off" Enabled="off">
        <Prompt>Controller type</Prompt>
        <Value>Unknown controller</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="server_type" Type="popup" Visible="off">
        <Prompt>Server type</Prompt>
        <Value>TCP</Value>
        <Callback>func = get_param(gcb,&apos;server_type&apos;);
p=Simulink.Mask.get(gcb);
a=p.getDialogControl(&apos;can_container&apos;);

if( func == &quot;CAN&quot;)
    a.Visible = &apos;on&apos;;
else
    a.Visible = &apos;off&apos;;
end
</Callback>
        <TypeOptions>
          <Option>TCP</Option>
          <Option>UDP</Option>
          <Option>CAN</Option>
          <Option>Bluetooth</Option>
        </TypeOptions>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="can_if" Type="popup" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>CAN bus</Prompt>
        <Value>CAN1 - Connector C pin 14 (L) and pin 15 (H)</Value>
        <TypeOptions>
          <Option>CAN1 - Connector C pin 14 (L) and pin 15 (H)</Option>
          <Option>CAN2 - Connector C pin 20 (L) and pin 21 (H)</Option>
          <Option>CAN3 - Connector C pin 19 (L) and pin 18 (H)</Option>
          <Option>CAN4 - Connector C pin 13 (L) and pin 12 (H)</Option>
          <Option>CAN1 - Connector B pin 24 (L) and pin 25 (H)</Option>
          <Option>CAN2 - Connector A pin 24 (L) and pin 25 (H)</Option>
          <Option>CAN1 - Connector pin 16 (L) and pin 17 (H)</Option>
          <Option>CAN2 - Connector pin 24 (L) and pin 25 (H)</Option>
        </TypeOptions>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="receive_id" Type="edit">
        <Prompt>Receive ID</Prompt>
        <Value>hex2dec(&apos;665&apos;)</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="receive_id_ext" Type="checkbox">
        <Prompt>Extended ID</Prompt>
        <Value>off</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="send_id" Type="edit">
        <Prompt>Send ID</Prompt>
        <Value>hex2dec(&apos;666&apos;)</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="send_id_ext" Type="checkbox">
        <Prompt>Extended ID</Prompt>
        <Value>off</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Parameters</Prompt>
        <ControlOptions Visible="off"/>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="ContrType">
        <Prompt>Controller type</Prompt>
        <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Popup" Name="server_type">
        <Prompt>Server type</Prompt>
        <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="can_container">
        <Prompt>CAN Settings</Prompt>
        <ControlOptions Visible="off"/>
        <DialogControl Type="Popup" Name="can_if">
          <Prompt>CAN bus</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="Container4">
          <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="receive_id">
            <Prompt>Receive ID</Prompt>
            <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
          </DialogControl>
          <DialogControl Type="CheckBox" Name="receive_id_ext">
            <Prompt>Extended ID</Prompt>
          </DialogControl>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="Container5">
          <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="send_id">
            <Prompt>Send ID</Prompt>
            <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
          </DialogControl>
          <DialogControl Type="CheckBox" Name="send_id_ext">
            <Prompt>Extended ID</Prompt>
          </DialogControl>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
  </Block>
</System>

__MWOPC_PART_BEGIN__ /simulink/systems/system_4032.xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<System>
  <P Name="Location">[2563, 1084, 3697, 2071]</P>
  <P Name="PaperType">usletter</P>
  <P Name="ZoomFactor">175</P>
  <Block BlockType="M-S-Function" Name="Memory read" SID="4104">
    <PortCounts out="1"/>
    <P Name="Position">[485, 585, 640, 635]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">101</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <List ListType="RTWdata">
      <P Name="memRead">1</P>
      <P Name="memType">1</P>
      <P Name="key">key</P>
      <P Name="init">0</P>
    </List>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_memory_emulation_read</P>
    <P Name="Parameters">tsamp</P>
    <Mask SelfModifiable="on">
      <Type>Read value from memory</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;Read from memory\nKey: %s&apos;,key);
text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Read from Memory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
This function block reads a value from non-volatile memory using the specified key.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
To store a value in memory, use the Write to Memory function block.
&lt;/p&gt;</Description>
      <Initialization>mdl = bdroot;
cs  = getActiveConfigSet(mdl);
try
t = go_target_name(get_param(cs,&apos;tlcGOcontrollTarget&apos;));
catch
t = &quot;Unknown controller&quot;;
end
msk = Simulink.Mask.get(gcb);
c = msk.getParameter(&apos;ContrType&apos;);
m = msk.getParameter(&apos;memType&apos;);
c.Value = t;

if contains(t,&apos;Moduline S1&apos;)
   m.TypeOptions = {&apos;Persistant Memory (eMMC)&apos;};
   m.Enabled = &apos;off&apos;;
end

    % update RTWdata so WriteRTW gets called when building the model
    modelRTWFields = 	struct( &apos;memRead&apos;, int2str(memRead), &apos;memType&apos;, int2str(memType),&apos;key&apos;, key, &apos;init&apos;, int2str(init));
    
    % Insert modelRTWFields in the I/O block S-Function containing the Tag starting with &apos;HANcoder_TARGET_&apos;
    HANcoder_TARGET_DataBlock = find_system(gcb, &apos;RegExp&apos;, &apos;on&apos;, &apos;FollowLinks&apos;, &apos;on&apos;, &apos;LookUnderMasks&apos;, &apos;all&apos;, &apos;BlockType&apos;, &apos;M-S-Function&apos;);
    set_param(HANcoder_TARGET_DataBlock{1}, &apos;RTWdata&apos;, modelRTWFields);</Initialization>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Read value from memory&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Reads a value that is stored on the controller under a name (key), for example a setting that has to survive a power cycle.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Key&lt;/b&gt;: the name of the value. A Memory write block with the same key and memory type stores it.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Memory type&lt;/b&gt;: &lt;i&gt;persistent&lt;/i&gt; survives a power cycle; &lt;i&gt;non-persistent&lt;/i&gt; is lost when the controller switches off; &lt;i&gt;configuration&lt;/i&gt; (Linux controllers) is a value that is set on the controller, for example through its web interface. The Moduline S1 has the persistent type only.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Memory read&lt;/b&gt;: once when the application starts, or periodically at the sample time.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Initialization value&lt;/b&gt;: the output as long as nothing is stored under the key yet.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;All controllers: Moduline S1, M1, L4 and HMI1. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/configuration/gocontroll-services/web-ui/simulink-configuration/&quot;&gt;Simulink Configuration in the web interface&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/configuration/gocontroll-services/web-ui/simulink-configuration/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="ContrType" Type="edit" Evaluate="off" Enabled="off">
        <Prompt>Controller type</Prompt>
        <Value>Unknown controller</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="memRead" Type="popup" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Memory read</Prompt>
        <Value>Read once during startup</Value>
        <TypeOptions>
          <Option>Read once during startup</Option>
          <Option>Read periodic based on sample time</Option>
        </TypeOptions>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="memType" Type="popup" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Memory type</Prompt>
        <Value>Persistant Memory (eMMC)</Value>
        <TypeOptions>
          <Option>Persistant Memory (eMMC)</Option>
          <Option>Non-persistant Memory (RAM)</Option>
          <Option>Configuration (eMMC)</Option>
        </TypeOptions>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="tsamp" Type="edit" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
        <Value>1</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="key" Type="edit" Evaluate="off" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Key</Prompt>
        <Value>key</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="init" Type="edit" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Initialization value</Prompt>
        <Value>0</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Parameters</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="ContrType">
          <Prompt>Controller type</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Popup" Name="memRead">
          <Prompt>Memory read</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Popup" Name="memType">
          <Prompt>Memory type</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="tsamp">
          <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="key">
          <Prompt>Key</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="init">
          <Prompt>Initialization value</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
  </Block>
  <Block BlockType="M-S-Function" Name="Memory write" SID="4103">
    <PortCounts in="1"/>
    <P Name="Position">[485, 511, 640, 559]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">100</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <List ListType="RTWdata">
      <P Name="key">key</P>
      <P Name="memType">1</P>
    </List>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_memory_emulation_write</P>
    <P Name="Parameters">tsamp</P>
    <Mask SelfModifiable="on">
      <Type>Store data to memory</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;Store in memory\nKey: %s&apos;,key);
text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Write to Memory&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
This function block stores a value in non-volatile memory using a specified key.
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;
To retrieve a stored value, use the Read from Memory function block and
provide the corresponding key.
&lt;/p&gt;
</Description>
      <Initialization>mdl = bdroot;
cs  = getActiveConfigSet(mdl);
try
t = go_target_name(get_param(cs,&apos;tlcGOcontrollTarget&apos;));
catch
t = &quot;Unknown controller&quot;;
end
msk = Simulink.Mask.get(gcb);
c = msk.getParameter(&apos;ContrType&apos;);
m = msk.getParameter(&apos;memType&apos;);
c.Value = t;

if contains(t,&apos;Moduline S1&apos;)
   m.TypeOptions = {&apos;Persistant Memory (eMMC)&apos;};
   m.Enabled = &apos;off&apos;;
end



    %update RTWdata so WriteRTW param gets called again
    modelRTWFields = struct(&apos;key&apos;, key,  &apos;memType&apos;, int2str(memType));

    % Insert modelRTWFields in the I/O block S-Function containing the Tag starting with &apos;HANcoder_TARGET_&apos;
    HANcoder_TARGET_DataBlock = find_system(gcb, &apos;RegExp&apos;, &apos;on&apos;, &apos;FollowLinks&apos;, &apos;on&apos;, &apos;LookUnderMasks&apos;, &apos;all&apos;, &apos;BlockType&apos;, &apos;M-S-Function&apos;);
    set_param(HANcoder_TARGET_DataBlock{1}, &apos;RTWdata&apos;, modelRTWFields);</Initialization>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Store data to memory&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stores the value on its input on the controller under a name (key), so a Memory read block can read it back, also after a power cycle.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Key&lt;/b&gt;: the name of the value. Use the same key and memory type in the Memory read block.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Memory type&lt;/b&gt;: &lt;i&gt;persistent&lt;/i&gt; survives a power cycle; &lt;i&gt;non-persistent&lt;/i&gt; is lost when the controller switches off. The Moduline S1 has the persistent type only.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Persistent memory wears with every write. Write when a value changes or at shutdown, for example in a triggered subsystem, not every sample.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;To keep values at shutdown: hold the controller on with &lt;i&gt;Controller Active&lt;/i&gt;, write, then release.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;All controllers: Moduline S1, M1, L4 and HMI1. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="ContrType" Type="edit" Evaluate="off" Enabled="off">
        <Prompt>Controller type</Prompt>
        <Value>Unknown controller</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="memType" Type="popup" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Memory type</Prompt>
        <Value>Persistant Memory (eMMC)</Value>
        <TypeOptions>
          <Option>Persistant Memory (eMMC)</Option>
          <Option>Non-persistant Memory (RAM)</Option>
        </TypeOptions>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="tsamp" Type="edit" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
        <Value>1</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="key" Type="edit" Evaluate="off" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Key</Prompt>
        <Value>key</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Parameters</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="ContrType">
          <Prompt>Controller type</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Popup" Name="memType">
          <Prompt>Memory type</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="tsamp">
          <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="key">
          <Prompt>Key</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
  </Block>
</System>

__MWOPC_PART_BEGIN__ /simulink/systems/system_4035.xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<System>
  <P Name="Location">[0, 0, 1920, 2160]</P>
  <P Name="PaperType">usletter</P>
  <P Name="ZoomFactor">300</P>
  <Block BlockType="SubSystem" Name="Delete all codes for one group" SID="4294">
    <PortCounts trigger="1"/>
    <P Name="Position">[600, 495, 840, 530]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">115</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <P Name="ContentPreviewEnabled">on</P>
    <Mask SelfModifiable="on">
      <Type>Delete diagnostic codes from memory</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;Delete all DTCs&apos;);
text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>This function block deletes all stored codes.</Description>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Delete diagnostic codes from memory&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Deletes all stored diagnostic trouble codes when it is triggered.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Connect the trigger to, for example, a service command received over CAN or a parameter set over XCP.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;All controllers: Moduline S1, M1, L4 and HMI1. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/faults/&quot;&gt;Diagnostic codes (Faults)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/faults/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="TriggerType" Type="promote" Evaluate="off" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Simulink:blkprm_prompts:TrigPortTrigType</Prompt>
        <Value>rising</Value>
        <TypeOptions>
          <Option>Trigger/TriggerType</Option>
        </TypeOptions>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Simulink:studio:ToolBarParametersMenu</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Popup" Name="TriggerType">
          <Prompt>Trigger type:</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
    <System Ref="system_4294"/>
  </Block>
  <Block BlockType="SubSystem" Name="Delete single DTC code" SID="4295">
    <PortCounts in="2" trigger="1"/>
    <P Name="Position">[605, 571, 840, 624]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">118</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <P Name="TreatAsAtomicUnit">on</P>
    <Mask SelfModifiable="on">
      <Type>Delete a single DTC from memory</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;Delete single DTC from memory&apos;);
port_label(&apos;input&apos;, 1, &apos;SPN&apos;);
port_label(&apos;input&apos;, 2, &apos;FMI&apos;);
text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>This function block deletes one DTC from memory:

SPN number:
A code to identify which part has failed

FMI:
How the part has failed</Description>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Delete a single DTC from memory&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Deletes one stored diagnostic trouble code when it is triggered.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Inputs: the SPN and the FMI of the code to delete.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The trigger input deletes the code.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;All controllers: Moduline S1, M1, L4 and HMI1. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/faults/&quot;&gt;Diagnostic codes (Faults)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/faults/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="TriggerType" Type="promote" Evaluate="off" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Simulink:blkprm_prompts:TrigPortTrigType</Prompt>
        <Value>rising</Value>
        <TypeOptions>
          <Option>Trigger/TriggerType</Option>
        </TypeOptions>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Simulink:studio:ToolBarParametersMenu</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Popup" Name="TriggerType">
          <Prompt>Trigger type:</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
    <System Ref="system_4295"/>
  </Block>
  <Block BlockType="SubSystem" Name="Diagnostic Helpers" SID="4338">
    <PortCounts/>
    <P Name="Position">[350, 454, 535, 511]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">120</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <P Name="UserDataPersistent">on</P>
    <Mask>
      <Display IconOpaque="transparent" RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;Diagnostic Helpers&apos;);</Display>
    </Mask>
    <System Ref="system_4338"/>
  </Block>
  <Block BlockType="M-S-Function" Name="Number of stored diagnostic codes" SID="4296">
    <PortCounts out="1"/>
    <P Name="Position">[600, 413, 840, 457]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">114</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <List ListType="RTWdata">
      <P Name="diagType">1</P>
    </List>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_memory_diagnostic_nrcodes_read</P>
    <P Name="Parameters">tsamp</P>
    <Mask SelfModifiable="on">
      <Type>Read number of stored codes</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;Get number of stored DTCs&apos;);
text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>This function block reads the number of stored codes.

Sample time:
Execution period for the function block.
You might want to put this block in a triggered subsystem or a function call subsystem</Description>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Read number of stored codes&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Outputs how many diagnostic trouble codes are stored on the controller.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use it for a warning light or to report over CAN that there are stored faults.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;All controllers: Moduline S1, M1, L4 and HMI1. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/faults/&quot;&gt;Diagnostic codes (Faults)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/faults/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="tsamp" Type="edit" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
        <Value>0.5</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Simulink:studio:ToolBarParametersMenu</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="tsamp">
          <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
  </Block>
  <Block BlockType="SubSystem" Name="Store diagnostic code" SID="4298">
    <PortCounts trigger="1"/>
    <P Name="Position">[605, 324, 840, 376]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">117</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <P Name="TreatAsAtomicUnit">on</P>
    <Mask SelfModifiable="on">
      <Type>Store diagnostic code to memory</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;Store DTC to memory\n SPN: %d\n FMI: %d&apos;,spn, fmi);
text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>This function block stores a diagnostic code to memory.

SPN number:
A code to identify which part has failed

FMI:
How the part has failed</Description>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Store diagnostic code to memory&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Stores a diagnostic trouble code on the controller when it is triggered. A code is an SPN (which part) with an FMI (how it failed).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;SPN number&lt;/b&gt;: the number of the part or signal.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Failure Mode Indicator&lt;/b&gt;: the kind of failure, one of the 23 J1939 failure modes (0 to 22).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The trigger input stores the code; by default on a rising edge.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Stored codes stay on the controller until they are deleted with one of the delete blocks.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;All controllers: Moduline S1, M1, L4 and HMI1. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/faults/&quot;&gt;Diagnostic codes (Faults)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/faults/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="spn" Type="promote">
        <Prompt>SPN number</Prompt>
        <Value>1234</Value>
        <TypeOptions>
          <Option>Store DTC code/spn</Option>
        </TypeOptions>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="fmi" Type="promote">
        <Prompt>Failure Mode Indicator</Prompt>
        <Value>(0) Data valid but above normal operational range, most severe level (3)</Value>
        <TypeOptions>
          <Option>Store DTC code/fmi</Option>
        </TypeOptions>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="TriggerType" Type="promote" Evaluate="off" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Simulink:blkprm_prompts:TrigPortTrigType</Prompt>
        <Value>rising</Value>
        <TypeOptions>
          <Option>Trigger/TriggerType</Option>
        </TypeOptions>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Simulink:studio:ToolBarParametersMenu</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="spn">
          <Prompt>SPN number</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Popup" Name="fmi">
          <Prompt>Failure Mode Indicator</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Popup" Name="TriggerType">
          <Prompt>Trigger type:</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
    <System Ref="system_4298"/>
  </Block>
</System>

__MWOPC_PART_BEGIN__ /simulink/systems/system_4051.xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<System>
  <P Name="Location">[2661, 1122, 3795, 2098]</P>
  <P Name="PaperType">usletter</P>
  <P Name="ZoomFactor">57</P>
  <Block BlockType="M-S-Function" Name="LIN Master" SID="4115">
    <PortCounts in="2"/>
    <P Name="Position">[-30, 96, 90, 354]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">52</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <List ListType="RTWdata">
      <P Name="id">1</P>
      <P Name="direction">2</P>
      <P Name="dataLength">1</P>
      <P Name="check">1</P>
    </List>
    <P Name="CopyFcn">go_block_platform_check(gcb, &apos;Linux&apos;, &apos;notify&apos;);</P>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_lin_master</P>
    <P Name="Parameters">tsamp, direction, dataLength</P>
    <Mask SelfModifiable="on">
      <Type>LIN Master</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;Master LIN\nmessage\nID: 0x%x&apos;,id);
text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());
if direction == 1
    port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 1, &apos;byte 1&apos;);
    port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 2, &apos;byte 2&apos;);
    if dataLength &gt; 1
        port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 3, &apos;byte 3&apos;);
        port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 4, &apos;byte 4&apos;);
    end
    if dataLength &gt; 2
        port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 5, &apos;byte 5&apos;);
        port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 6, &apos;byte 6&apos;);
        port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 7, &apos;byte 7&apos;);
        port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 8, &apos;byte 8&apos;);
    end
else
    port_label(&apos;input&apos;, 1, &apos;byte 1&apos;);
    port_label(&apos;input&apos;, 2, &apos;byte 2&apos;);
    if dataLength &gt; 1
        port_label(&apos;input&apos;, 3, &apos;byte 3&apos;);
        port_label(&apos;input&apos;, 4, &apos;byte 4&apos;);
    end
    if dataLength &gt; 2
        port_label(&apos;input&apos;, 5, &apos;byte 5&apos;);
        port_label(&apos;input&apos;, 6, &apos;byte 6&apos;);
        port_label(&apos;input&apos;, 7, &apos;byte 7&apos;);
        port_label(&apos;input&apos;, 8, &apos;byte 8&apos;);
    end
end</Display>
      <Description>Function
==========
This block implements the LIN master functionality for communication with LIN 
slaves. The block complies with LIN 1.3 an LIN 2.0. When sending data to a slave 
device, this block will add the data to the LIN bus. When retrieving data from slaves, The block will wait for incoming data over LIN.

Parameters
========== 
Identifier: 
Selects the identifier to communicate with

Direction: 
Request data from a slave device or send data to a slave device

Datalength:
Defines the number of bytes that need to be send to- or requested from the slave 

Checksum: 
Select Classic for checksum based on databytes only. Enhanced for databytes and 
ID byte

Sample time:
Defines the execution interval of the block.

Input
==========
Port 1..8               LIN Data bytes to be send to a slave

Output
==========
Port 1..8               LIN Data bytes that are received from the slave&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;For the Linux controllers (Moduline M1, L4, HMI1) only.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</Description>
      <Initialization>go_block_platform_check(gcb, &apos;Linux&apos;);
% Create resource keywords to be reserved in resource database
modelRTWFields = struct(&apos;id&apos;, int2str(id), &apos;direction&apos;, int2str(direction),&apos;dataLength&apos;, int2str(dataLength),&apos;check&apos;, int2str(check));

% Insert modelRTWFields in the I/O block S-Function containing the Tag starting with &apos;HANcoder_TARGET_&apos;
HANcoder_TARGET_DataBlock = find_system(gcb, &apos;RegExp&apos;, &apos;on&apos;, &apos;FollowLinks&apos;, &apos;on&apos;, &apos;LookUnderMasks&apos;, &apos;all&apos;, &apos;BlockType&apos;, &apos;M-S-Function&apos;);
set_param(HANcoder_TARGET_DataBlock{1}, &apos;RTWdata&apos;, modelRTWFields);</Initialization>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;LIN Master&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sends or requests one LIN frame as the master of a LIN bus (LIN 1.3 and 2.0).&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Identifier&lt;/b&gt;: the identifier of the frame, 0x01 and up.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Direction&lt;/b&gt;: &lt;i&gt;send&lt;/i&gt; transmits the data on the inputs; &lt;i&gt;request&lt;/i&gt; asks a slave for the frame and puts its data on the outputs.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Data Length&lt;/b&gt;: 2, 4 or 8 bytes. &lt;b&gt;Checksum&lt;/b&gt;: Classic or Enhanced, as the slave expects.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Use one block per frame.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Linux controllers only: Moduline M1, L4 and HMI1. In a model for the Moduline S1 the block gives an error. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/l4/&quot;&gt;Moduline L4&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/l4/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="id" Type="popup" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Identifier</Prompt>
        <Value>0x01</Value>
        <TypeOptions>
          <Option>0x01</Option>
          <Option>0x02</Option>
          <Option>0x03</Option>
          <Option>0x04</Option>
          <Option>0x05</Option>
          <Option>0x06</Option>
          <Option>0x07</Option>
          <Option>0x08</Option>
          <Option>0x09</Option>
          <Option>0x0A</Option>
          <Option>0x0B</Option>
          <Option>0x0C</Option>
          <Option>0x0D</Option>
          <Option>0x0E</Option>
          <Option>0x0F</Option>
          <Option>0x10</Option>
          <Option>0x11</Option>
          <Option>0x12</Option>
          <Option>0x13</Option>
          <Option>0x14</Option>
          <Option>0x15</Option>
          <Option>0x16</Option>
          <Option>0x17</Option>
          <Option>0x18</Option>
          <Option>0x19</Option>
          <Option>0x1A</Option>
          <Option>0x1B</Option>
          <Option>0x1C</Option>
          <Option>0x1D</Option>
          <Option>0x1E</Option>
          <Option>0x1F</Option>
          <Option>0x20</Option>
          <Option>0x21</Option>
          <Option>0x22</Option>
          <Option>0x23</Option>
          <Option>0x24</Option>
          <Option>0x25</Option>
          <Option>0x26</Option>
          <Option>0x27</Option>
          <Option>0x28</Option>
          <Option>0x29</Option>
          <Option>0x2A</Option>
          <Option>0x2B</Option>
          <Option>0x2C</Option>
          <Option>0x2D</Option>
          <Option>0x2E</Option>
          <Option>0x2F</Option>
          <Option>0x30</Option>
          <Option>0x31</Option>
          <Option>0x32</Option>
          <Option>0x33</Option>
          <Option>0x34</Option>
          <Option>0x35</Option>
          <Option>0x36</Option>
          <Option>0x37</Option>
          <Option>0x38</Option>
          <Option>0x39</Option>
          <Option>0x3A</Option>
          <Option>0x3B</Option>
          <Option>0x3C (diagnostic)</Option>
          <Option>0x3D (diagnostic)</Option>
          <Option>0x3E (reserved)</Option>
          <Option>0x3F (reserved)</Option>
        </TypeOptions>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="direction" Type="popup" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Direction</Prompt>
        <Value>Send data</Value>
        <TypeOptions>
          <Option>Request data</Option>
          <Option>Send data</Option>
        </TypeOptions>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="dataLength" Type="popup" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Data Length</Prompt>
        <Value>2</Value>
        <TypeOptions>
          <Option>2</Option>
          <Option>4</Option>
          <Option>8</Option>
        </TypeOptions>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="check" Type="popup" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Checksum</Prompt>
        <Value>Classic (LIN 1.3)</Value>
        <TypeOptions>
          <Option>Classic (LIN 1.3)</Option>
          <Option>Enhanced (LIN 2.0)</Option>
        </TypeOptions>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="tsamp" Type="edit" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
        <Value>-1</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Simulink:studio:ToolBarParametersMenu</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Popup" Name="id">
          <Prompt>Identifier</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Popup" Name="direction">
          <Prompt>Direction</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Popup" Name="dataLength">
          <Prompt>Data Length</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Popup" Name="check">
          <Prompt>Checksum</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="tsamp">
          <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
  </Block>
</System>

__MWOPC_PART_BEGIN__ /simulink/systems/system_4065.xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<System>
  <P Name="Location">[2673, 1032, 3807, 2091]</P>
  <P Name="PaperType">usletter</P>
  <P Name="ZoomFactor">144</P>
  <Block BlockType="M-S-Function" Name="UDP Configure" SID="4091">
    <PortCounts/>
    <P Name="Position">[1070, 425, 1225, 495]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">474</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <List ListType="RTWdata">
      <P Name="port">9001</P>
      <P Name="ip">0.0.0.0</P>
      <P Name="broadcast">1</P>
      <P Name="socket_id">id</P>
    </List>
    <P Name="CopyFcn">go_block_platform_check(gcb, &apos;Linux&apos;, &apos;notify&apos;);</P>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_UDPConfig</P>
    <Mask SelfModifiable="on">
      <Type>UDP Configure</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;Configure UDP socket\n IP: %s\nPort: %d\n%s&apos;,ip,port,broadcastStr);
text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>Block to configure a UDP connection

The socket ID should be a unique identifier to link the send and receive blocks to.
The name of the actual socket in the C code will be socket_&lt;socket id&gt;, so characters that would not work in a C variable name will not work.

Setting the ip to 0.0.0.0 makes the controller accept messages on all interfaces.
Set it to the ip of a specific interface to limit this.

Allowing broadcasting enables you to send messages to a full range of ip addresses, for example:
192.168.255.255 sends messages to 192.168.1.1, 192.168.2.1 ... 192.168.1.2, 192.168.1.3...&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;For the Linux controllers (Moduline M1, L4, HMI1) only.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</Description>
      <Initialization>go_block_platform_check(gcb, &apos;Linux&apos;);
    if broadcast == 0
        broadcastStr = &quot;Not broadcasting&quot;;
    else
        broadcastStr = &quot;Broadcasting&quot;;
    end
    if ~is_ip(ip)
        error(&apos;Entered IP is not valid&apos;);
    end
    if mod(port,1) &gt; 0 || port &lt; intmin(&apos;uint16&apos;) || port &gt; intmax(&apos;uint16&apos;)
        error(&apos;Entered Port is not valid, it should be an integer from 0-65335&apos;);
    end

    blockPath = split(gcb, &apos;/&apos;);
    configures = find_system(blockPath(1),&apos;RegExp&apos;, &apos;on&apos;,&apos;FollowLinks&apos;, &apos;on&apos;,&apos;MaskType&apos;,&apos;UDP Configure&apos;);
    options = cell(1,length(configures));
    for idx = 1:length(configures)
        options(idx) = get_param(configures(idx),&apos;socket_id&apos;);
    end

    if length(unique(options)) ~= length(options)
        error(&apos;Socket id is already in use, set a unique socket id&apos;);
    end

	modelRTWFields = struct(&apos;port&apos;, num2str(port), &apos;ip&apos;, ip, &apos;broadcast&apos;, num2str(broadcast), &apos;socket_id&apos;, socket_id);

	% Insert modelRTWFields in the I/O block S-Function containing the Tag starting with &apos;HANcoder_TARGET_&apos;
	HANcoder_TARGET_DataBlock = find_system(gcb, &apos;RegExp&apos;, &apos;on&apos;, &apos;FollowLinks&apos;, &apos;on&apos;, &apos;LookUnderMasks&apos;, &apos;all&apos;, &apos;BlockType&apos;, &apos;M-S-Function&apos;);
	set_param(HANcoder_TARGET_DataBlock{1}, &apos;RTWdata&apos;, modelRTWFields);</Initialization>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;UDP Configure&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Opens a UDP socket. The UDP Receive and UDP Send blocks use it by its name.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Socket id&lt;/b&gt;: a name for this socket; give the same name in the receive and send blocks.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The port and address the socket listens on. &lt;b&gt;Allow broadcasting&lt;/b&gt; lets the socket send to a broadcast address.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The &lt;i&gt;UDP Example&lt;/i&gt; in the library shows the complete pattern with Byte Pack and Byte Unpack.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Linux controllers only: Moduline M1, L4 and HMI1. In a model for the Moduline S1 the block gives an error. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="socket_id" Type="edit" Evaluate="off" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Socket id</Prompt>
        <Value>id</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="port" Type="edit" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>The port on which to listen/send</Prompt>
        <Value>9001</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="ip" Type="edit">
        <Prompt>The ip on which to listen/send</Prompt>
        <Value>&apos;0.0.0.0&apos;</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="broadcast" Type="checkbox">
        <Prompt>Allow broadcasting of sent messages</Prompt>
        <Value>on</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Parameters</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="socket_id">
          <Prompt>Socket id</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="port">
          <Prompt>The port on which to listen/send</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="ip">
          <Prompt>The ip on which to listen/send</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="CheckBox" Name="broadcast">
          <Prompt>Allow broadcasting of sent messages</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
  </Block>
  <Block BlockType="SubSystem" Name="UDP Example" SID="4175">
    <PortCounts/>
    <P Name="Position">[1070, 734, 1225, 816]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">476</P>
    <P Name="HideAutomaticName">off</P>
    <System Ref="system_4175"/>
  </Block>
  <Block BlockType="S-Function" Name="UDP Receive" SID="4092">
    <PortCounts out="3"/>
    <P Name="Position">[1070, 524, 1225, 596]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">475</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <P Name="CopyFcn">go_block_platform_check(gcb, &apos;Linux&apos;, &apos;notify&apos;);</P>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_UDPReceive</P>
    <P Name="Parameters">buff_len,socket_id,tsamp</P>
    <P Name="SFunctionDeploymentMode">off</P>
    <P Name="EnableBusSupport">off</P>
    <P Name="SFcnIsStateOwnerBlock">off</P>
    <Mask SelfModifiable="on">
      <Type>UDP Receive</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;UDP Receive&apos;);
text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 1, &apos;function call&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 2, &apos;message&apos;);
port_label(&apos;output&apos;, 3, &apos;message length&apos;);</Display>
      <Description>Receive all UDP messages

For every message received this block will call the functions attached to the function call output.
In these function calls you can then use the message and message length outputs to process/buffer the received messages.

Outputs:
function call:
Attach to a function call subsystem or something like it to call that function every time a message is received.

message:
The uint8 vector received from the socket. The length of this vector is likely longer than the actual number of bytes received.

message length:
The number of bytes actually received, use this to get the actual fresh bytes from the message.

Parameters:
buffer size:
The maximum number of bytes that can be read from the socket in one message, this also determines the width of the message vector.&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;For the Linux controllers (Moduline M1, L4, HMI1) only.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</Description>
      <Initialization>go_block_platform_check(gcb, &apos;Linux&apos;);
</Initialization>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;UDP Receive&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Receives UDP messages on a socket made with &lt;i&gt;UDP Configure&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Choose the socket of the UDP Configure block.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Outputs: a function call for each received message, the message (uint8 vector) and its length.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Process the message in a function-call subsystem.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Linux controllers only: Moduline M1, L4 and HMI1. In a model for the Moduline S1 the block gives an error. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="tsamp" Type="edit">
        <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
        <Value>-1</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="socket_id" Type="combobox" Evaluate="off" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Socket</Prompt>
        <Value>id</Value>
        <Callback>blockPath = split(gcb, &apos;/&apos;);
configures = find_system(blockPath(1),&apos;RegExp&apos;, &apos;on&apos;,&apos;FollowLinks&apos;, &apos;on&apos;,&apos;MaskType&apos;,&apos;UDP Configure&apos;);
mask = Simulink.Mask.get(gcb);
pars = mask.Parameters;
options = cell(1,length(configures));
for idx = 1:length(configures)
    options(idx) = get_param(configures(idx),&apos;socket_id&apos;);
end
mask.getParameter(&apos;socket_id&apos;).TypeOptions = options;</Callback>
        <TypeOptions>
          <Option>id</Option>
          <Option>led_sinus</Option>
        </TypeOptions>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="buff_len" Type="edit" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Buffer size</Prompt>
        <Value>1</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Parameters</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="tsamp">
          <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="ComboBox" Name="socket_id">
          <Prompt>Socket</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="buff_len">
          <Prompt>Buffer size</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
  </Block>
  <Block BlockType="M-S-Function" Name="UDP Send" SID="4093">
    <PortCounts in="1"/>
    <P Name="Position">[1070, 627, 1225, 703]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">473</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <List ListType="RTWdata">
      <P Name="port">9001</P>
      <P Name="ip">0.0.0.0</P>
      <P Name="socket_id">id</P>
    </List>
    <P Name="CopyFcn">go_block_platform_check(gcb, &apos;Linux&apos;, &apos;notify&apos;);</P>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_UDPSend</P>
    <P Name="Parameters">tsamp,ip,port</P>
    <Mask SelfModifiable="on">
      <Type>UDP Send</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&apos;UDP Send\nIP: %s\nPort: %d&apos;,ip,port);
port_label(&apos;input&apos;, 1, &apos;message&apos;);
text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>Send a UDP message to the designated address.

The Message input should be a uint8 vector, if you end up with a [1xn] or [nx1] matrix, use the reshape block to turn it into a vector.

IP address should be a valid IP address as a string

Port should be a within the range of a uint16&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;For the Linux controllers (Moduline M1, L4, HMI1) only.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</Description>
      <Initialization>go_block_platform_check(gcb, &apos;Linux&apos;);
    if ~is_ip(ip)
        error(&apos;Entered IP is not valid&apos;);
    end
    if mod(port,1) &gt; 0 || port &lt; intmin(&apos;uint16&apos;) || port &gt; intmax(&apos;uint16&apos;)
        error(&apos;Entered Port is not valid, it should be an integer from 0-65335&apos;);
    end
    % update RTWdata to call WriteRTW again
    modelRTWFields = struct(&apos;port&apos;, num2str(port), &apos;ip&apos;, ip, &apos;socket_id&apos;, socket_id);

    % Insert modelRTWFields in the I/O block S-Function containing the Tag starting with &apos;HANcoder_TARGET_&apos;
    HANcoder_TARGET_DataBlock = find_system(gcb, &apos;RegExp&apos;, &apos;on&apos;, &apos;FollowLinks&apos;, &apos;on&apos;, &apos;LookUnderMasks&apos;, &apos;all&apos;, &apos;BlockType&apos;, &apos;M-S-Function&apos;);
    set_param(HANcoder_TARGET_DataBlock{1}, &apos;RTWdata&apos;, modelRTWFields);</Initialization>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;UDP Send&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sends a UDP message on a socket made with &lt;i&gt;UDP Configure&lt;/i&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Choose the socket of the UDP Configure block.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;IP address&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;port&lt;/b&gt;: where the message goes.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Input: the data as a uint8 vector. The sample time is the send rate.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Linux controllers only: Moduline M1, L4 and HMI1. In a model for the Moduline S1 the block gives an error. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="socket_id" Type="combobox" Evaluate="off">
        <Prompt>Socket</Prompt>
        <Value>id</Value>
        <Callback>blockPath = split(gcb, &apos;/&apos;);
configures = find_system(blockPath(1),&apos;RegExp&apos;, &apos;on&apos;,&apos;FollowLinks&apos;, &apos;on&apos;,&apos;MaskType&apos;,&apos;UDP Configure&apos;);
mask = Simulink.Mask.get(gcb);
pars = mask.Parameters;
options = cell(1,length(configures));
for idx = 1:length(configures)
    options(idx) = get_param(configures(idx),&apos;socket_id&apos;);
end
pars(1).TypeOptions = options;</Callback>
        <TypeOptions>
          <Option>id</Option>
          <Option>led_sinus</Option>
        </TypeOptions>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="ip" Type="edit">
        <Prompt>The IP address to send to</Prompt>
        <Value>&apos;0.0.0.0&apos;</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="port" Type="edit">
        <Prompt>The port to send to</Prompt>
        <Value>9001</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <MaskParameter Name="tsamp" Type="edit">
        <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
        <Value>1</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Simulink:studio:ToolBarParametersMenu</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="ComboBox" Name="socket_id">
          <Prompt>Socket</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="ip">
          <Prompt>The IP address to send to</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="port">
          <Prompt>The port to send to</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="tsamp">
          <Prompt>Sample time</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
  </Block>
</System>

__MWOPC_PART_BEGIN__ /simulink/systems/system_4089.xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<System>
  <P Name="Location">[3912, 0, 7680, 2160]</P>
  <P Name="PaperType">usletter</P>
  <P Name="ZoomFactor">374</P>
  <Block BlockType="M-S-Function" Name="Set display brightness" SID="4098">
    <PortCounts in="1"/>
    <P Name="Position">[70, 114, 215, 166]</P>
    <P Name="ZOrder">16</P>
    <P Name="BackgroundColor">[1.000000, 0.666667, 0.000000]</P>
    <P Name="CopyFcn">go_block_platform_check(gcb, &apos;Linux&apos;, &apos;notify&apos;);</P>
    <P Name="FunctionName">sfcn_set_brightness_display</P>
    <P Name="Parameters">tsamp</P>
    <Mask>
      <Type>Set display brightness</Type>
      <Display RunInitForIconRedraw="on" IconUnits="pixels">fprintf(&quot;Set display brightness&quot;);
text(2, 6, GOcontroll_Simulink_version());</Display>
      <Description>Set the brightness of a display (only works with the max25014 driver currently)
Keeps the original brightness untill the first non zero value is received&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;For the Linux controllers (Moduline M1, L4, HMI1) only.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</Description>
      <Initialization>go_block_platform_check(gcb, &apos;Linux&apos;);
</Initialization>
      <Help>&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;font-family:sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Set display brightness&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Sets the brightness of the display of the Moduline HMI1.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;How to use it&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Input: the brightness.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The display keeps its original brightness until the first value above 0 arrives.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Controllers&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;p&gt;Moduline HMI1. In a model for the Moduline S1 the block gives an error. The greyed-out field &lt;i&gt;Controller type&lt;/i&gt;, when the block has one, shows the controller chosen under &lt;i&gt;Configuration Parameters &amp;gt; Code Generation &amp;gt; GOcontroll options &amp;gt; Target&lt;/i&gt;; the choices in the block follow it.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;h3&gt;GOcontroll knowledge base&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/hmi1/&quot;&gt;Moduline HMI1&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/modular-hardware/controllers/hmi1/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&quot;&gt;Using the blockset&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;https://gocontroll.com/knowledge-base/getting-started/programming/simulink/blockset-information/&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</Help>
      <MaskParameter Name="tsamp" Type="edit" Tunable="off">
        <Prompt>Sample time:</Prompt>
        <Value>1</Value>
      </MaskParameter>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="DescGroupVar">
        <Prompt>%&lt;MaskType&gt;</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Text" Name="DescTextVar">
          <Prompt>%&lt;MaskDescription&gt;</Prompt>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
      <DialogControl Type="Group" Name="ParameterGroupVar">
        <Prompt>Parameters</Prompt>
        <DialogControl Type="Edit" Name="tsamp">
          <Prompt>Sample time:</Prompt>
          <ControlOptions PromptLocation="left"/>
        </DialogControl>
      </DialogControl>
    </Mask>
  </Block>
</System>

